From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:47:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Build with Soong

The Android image build compiles eSpeak NG from this tree with Soong, as
it does the other applications it ships. The Android.bp lists the
sources the CMake build compiles for the Android build (async speech,
MBROLA and PCAudio off; libsonic, klatt and speechPlayer on) as static
libraries for the device and for the host, with the config.h each of
them gets, and builds libttsespeak and the app from android/. A host
build of the command line program compiles the voice data as
cmake/data.cmake does, and a genrule zips it with its SHA-256 into the
raw resources the Gradle build makes. The Gradle files are not used.

The pinned libsonic tree is placed in sonic/ beside these sources before
the build; it is not part of this series. The BuildConfig the Gradle
build generates and the manifest with the package it sets as the
namespace are written beside the sources, in android/soong. The manifest
leaves out the uses-library of the Wear OS shared library, which the
platform does not have and the app does not require.

The compat <stdio.h> includes the system one outside its include
guard: glibc's <wchar.h> before 2.28 includes <stdio.h> for the FILE
types only and expects it to be included again, which the guard of the
shim turned into the only inclusion (the host libraries are built
against a glibc 2.17 sysroot). The speechPlayer sources are built with
-Wnon-virtual-dtor as a warning, which the platform's C++ flags make an
error, and the data tool carries its C++ library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
